3
00:00:11,141 --> 00:00:12,795
MR. NORRIS,
I'M GONNA LET ONE OF MY GUYS

4
00:00:12,795 --> 00:00:14,536
SHOW YOU THE LAMBORGHINI.

5
00:00:14,536 --> 00:00:17,104
IT'S YOUR NEW CAR.
YOU JUST DON'T KNOW IT YET.

6
00:00:17,104 --> 00:00:19,715
THE McLAREN LOOKS GOOD ON YOU,
MR. LANDAU.NOT TONIGHT.

7
00:00:19,715 --> 00:00:22,718
A LOT OF FELLAS OUT THERE--

8
00:00:22,718 --> 00:00:25,112
THEY'VE GOT TO SELL
STATION WAGONS, MINIVANS,

9
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:27,897
THIS?
I DON'T HAVE TO SELL THIS.

10
00:00:27,897 --> 00:00:30,856
[trunk bell chirps]THIS IS THE GOOD LIFE
ON WHEELS, STEM TO STERN.

11
00:00:30,856 --> 00:00:34,643
HELL, THE TRUNK'S BIGGER
THAN MY FIRST APARTMENT.

12
00:00:34,643 --> 00:00:37,689
OH, MY GOD.

13
00:00:37,689 --> 00:00:39,952
LISELLE.

14
00:00:44,131 --> 00:00:46,176
AGENT RIGSBY,
WHAT DO WE HAVE?

15
00:00:46,176 --> 00:00:49,832
HEY, BOSS. LISELLE DOUGLAS,
SALESPERSON HERE, AGE 28.

16
00:00:49,832 --> 00:00:51,834
BLUNT FORCE TRAUMA,
NUMEROUS CONTUSIONS,

17
00:00:51,834 --> 00:00:54,097
POSSIBLE SKULL FRACTURE.HER CLOTHES ARE STILL INTACT.

18
00:00:54,097 --> 00:00:56,534
NO OBVIOUS SIGNS
OF SEXUAL ASSAULT.[sniffs] OH.

19
00:00:56,534 --> 00:00:59,842
WHAT IS IT?I JUST LOVE
THAT NEW CAR SMELL.

20
00:00:59,842 --> 00:01:03,367
ANYTHING
ON THE TIME OF DEATH?SHE WAS LAST SEEN WORKING HERE
LATE LAST NIGHT.

21
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:06,501
PRIVATE SECURITY
DID A SWEEP AT MIDNIGHT,

22
00:01:06,501 --> 00:01:09,939
REPORTED THE ALARM SYSTEM
HADN'T BEEN ACTIVATED.

23
00:01:09,939 --> 00:01:13,595
CORONER THINKS SHE WAS
PROBABLY DEAD BY THEN.LET'S GET THE BODY OUT OF HERE,
SEE WHAT WE CAN FIND OUT.

24
00:01:13,595 --> 00:01:16,032
[Rigsby] YEAH, YOU GOT IT.THAT'S EXPENSIVE, HUH?

25
00:01:16,032 --> 00:01:17,381
$300,000 RETAIL.

26
00:01:17,381 --> 00:01:19,470
PROBABLY GET
A DISCOUNT NOW, THOUGH.

27
00:01:23,561 --> 00:01:26,173
HEY, GUYS.
ONE OF YOU FOUND THE BODY?

28
00:01:26,173 --> 00:01:28,958
YEAH, JAMES KINSEY. I BELIEVE
HE'S IN THE JOHN RIGHT NOW.

29
00:01:28,958 --> 00:01:32,657
BRAD ELIAS.ANY IDEA WHO COULD HAVE
DONE THIS, MR. ELIAS?

30
00:01:32,657 --> 00:01:35,182
NO. NONE. IT WAS HORRIBLE.
THIS IS A TRAGEDY.

31
00:01:35,182 --> 00:01:38,098
WE'RE LIKE A FAMILY HERE.HA! FAMILY.

32
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:40,448
THAT'S CUTE.EXCUSE ME?

33
00:01:40,448 --> 00:01:42,711
YOU WORK ON COMMISSION,
RIGHT?

34
00:01:42,711 --> 00:01:46,497
SURE.OKAY, THEN YOU'RE NOT A FAMILY
AT ALL. YOU'RE A GLADIATOR PIT.

35
00:01:46,497 --> 00:01:48,195
YOU'RE A SEETHING MASS

36
00:01:48,195 --> 00:01:50,110
OF PRIMAL HOSTILITY
AND MISTRUST.

37
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:52,199
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

38
00:01:52,199 --> 00:01:54,201
PEOPLE HAVE THE WRONG IDEA
ABOUT SALES.

39
00:01:54,201 --> 00:01:57,943
THERE'S A LOT OF RESPECT
AMONG US, RIGHT, GUYS?[man] OH, YEAH.

40
00:01:57,943 --> 00:02:00,250
CLEARLY YOU'RE A TOP DOG
AMONGST THIS PACK HERE,

41
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:03,471
BUT THE QUESTION IS,
WHO'S THE FASTEST RUNNER?RUNNER?

42
00:02:03,471 --> 00:02:06,822
LISELLE'S CLIENTS ARE GONNA NEED
A NEW BROKER, AREN'T THEY?

43
00:02:06,822 --> 00:02:09,259
AND I THINK THAT MY ASSOCIATE,
AGENT CHO HERE,

44
00:02:09,259 --> 00:02:11,957
LEFT HER CLIENT LIST UPSTAIRS.
IN YOUR BREAK ROOM.

45
00:02:11,957 --> 00:02:15,265
IT MIGHT BE A LITTLE GHOULISH
TO GRAB IT UP SO SOON,

46
00:02:15,265 --> 00:02:18,007
BUT IT IS STILL UP THERE,
AND SOMEONE,

47
00:02:18,007 --> 00:02:21,053
AT SOME POINT, WILL...

48
00:02:21,053 --> 00:02:23,404
I'VE GOT THE CLIENT LIST
RIGHT HERE. IT'S EVIDENCE.

49
00:02:23,404 --> 00:02:25,449
WHAT DID YOU DO THAT FOR?

50
00:02:25,449 --> 00:02:28,452
I HAVE ELIMINATED THIS MAN
FROM ANY SUSPICION.

51
00:02:28,452 --> 00:02:31,673
TOO HONEST TO PROFIT FROM
A KILLING? TOO HONEST TO KILL.

52
00:02:31,673 --> 00:02:33,153
RIGHT?RIGHT.

53
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,024
[grunting]

54
00:02:35,024 --> 00:02:37,896
HEY, GUYS, BREAK IT UP.

55
00:02:37,896 --> 00:02:40,290
UNLESS, OF COURSE,
YOU'RE VERY CUNNING

56
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:43,206
AND YOU'RE WORKING
A DOUBLE BLUFF.[Cho] COME ON. TAKE IT--
HEY, COME ON.

57
00:02:43,206 --> 00:02:45,208
NO, I DIDN'T THINK SO.

58
00:02:45,208 --> 00:02:47,297
[Cho] COME ON. COME ON.

59
00:02:47,297 --> 00:03:00,005
COME ON. BREAK IT UP.
BREAK IT UP. COME ON, GUYS. HEY.

60
00:03:00,005 --> 00:03:02,443
LISELLE DIDN'T SHOW UP
FOR WORK YESTERDAY.

61
00:03:02,443 --> 00:03:05,228
I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT TO THINK.
IT WASN'T LIKE HER.

62
00:03:05,228 --> 00:03:06,838
YOU WERE WORRIED?

63
00:03:06,838 --> 00:03:09,841
I WAS PISSED. HOSTING THE PARTY
WAS HER RESPONSIBILITY.

64
00:03:09,841 --> 00:03:12,714
IT'S A GOOD THINK
THAT KINSEY STEPPED UP.

65
00:03:12,714 --> 00:03:15,282
HEARD YOU BOYS
DIDN'T PLAY NICE LAST NIGHT.

66
00:03:15,282 --> 00:03:17,284
NAUGHTY, NAUGHTY.

67
00:03:17,284 --> 00:03:19,677
YOU LIKE YOUR EMPLOYEES
AT EACH OTHER'S THROATS?

68
00:03:19,677 --> 00:03:22,289
YOU BET I DO.
THIS IS A JOB FOR WINNERS.

69
00:03:22,289 --> 00:03:24,682
WE'RE THE TOP LUXURY BROKER
IN NORTHERN CALIFORNIA.

70
00:03:24,682 --> 00:03:26,771
WE GOT FOUR FLOORS OF STOCK
BACK THERE.

71
00:03:26,771 --> 00:03:29,557
WE GOT OVER $100 MILLION
IN SALES ANNUALLY.

72
00:03:29,557 --> 00:03:32,908
MY GUYS HAVE TO EARN
THEIR PLACE.

73
00:03:32,908 --> 00:03:35,302
SO EVERY SIX MONTHS
WE HAVE A SALES DRIVE.

74
00:03:35,302 --> 00:03:38,653
[claps hands]TOP GUY ON THE BOARD GETS
A TITANIUM DIAMOND ROLEX.

75
00:03:38,653 --> 00:03:41,612
BOTTOM GUY...
GETS A NEW JOB.

76
00:03:41,612 --> 00:03:44,572
LOOK, AGENTS,

77
00:03:44,572 --> 00:03:48,140
NOT TO PRESS--MY CLIENTS WOULD
LIKE TO KNOW WHEN WE CAN REOPEN.

78
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:51,927
WHAT CAN I TELL THEM?YOU CAN TELL THEM
A WOMAN'S DEAD.

79
00:03:51,927 --> 00:03:55,191
WHICH IS TERRIBLE, UH,
BUT THIS IS A SERVICE BUSINESS.

80
00:03:55,191 --> 00:03:58,020
AND WHEN SHARKS STOP SWIMMING,
THEY DROWN, RIGHT?

81
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:05,332
[claps hands]NO MALINGERING, GUY.

82
00:04:05,332 --> 00:04:07,725
[chuckles]THIS IS JAMES KINSEY.

83
00:04:07,725 --> 00:04:10,206
AH.

84
00:04:10,206 --> 00:04:12,991
AH, TOP SALESMAN.
CONGRATULATIONS.

85
00:04:12,991 --> 00:04:15,820
THANKS.DAMN RIGHT. THIS GUY
COULD SELL A CAT TO A MOUSE.

86
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:20,172
AH, I MIGHT HAVE TO THROW IN
A FEW EXTRAS TO CLOSE THAT DEAL.[chuckles]

87
00:04:20,172 --> 00:04:23,219
MR. WESTHOFF HERE SAYS
YOU WERE WORKING WITH LISELLE

88
00:04:23,219 --> 00:04:26,309
THE NIGHT SHE DISAPPEARED.YEAH, WORKING
ON LAST NIGHT'S PARTY, SURE.

89
00:04:26,309 --> 00:04:29,312
I LEFT HER HERE
ABOUT, UH, 8:00, 8:30.HOW'D SHE SEEM--HER DEMEANOR?

90
00:04:29,312 --> 00:04:32,620
FINE, I GUESS.
UH, A LITTLE TENSE, MAYBE.

91
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:34,622
A LOT OF PRESSURE TO GET
THAT PARTY TOGETHER.

92
00:04:34,622 --> 00:04:37,407
HEY. HEY.
THAT--THAT'S--THAT'S MINE.

93
00:04:37,407 --> 00:04:38,800
THAT.

94
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,845
OKAY.

95
00:04:40,845 --> 00:04:42,760
NOW HOW'D YOU AND LISELLE
GET ALONG?

96
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:45,459
UH, GREAT.
SHE'S A GREAT GIRL.

97
00:04:45,459 --> 00:04:46,851
GREAT?

98
00:04:46,851 --> 00:04:49,680
BUT YOU RESENTED HER.NO.

99
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,813
YES.

100
00:04:51,813 --> 00:04:54,598
WHY WAS THAT? SHE WAS
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE PACK,

101
00:04:54,598 --> 00:04:57,079
SO SHE WAS NO THREAT TO YOU.

102
00:04:57,079 --> 00:05:00,517
LISELLE DID VERY WELL
FOR HER AGE.

103
00:05:00,517 --> 00:05:03,520
SHE DID VERY WELL
BECAUSE SHE WAS BEAUTIFUL,

104
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:05,740
AND YOU FELT THAT GAVE HER
AN UNFAIR ADVANTAGE.

105
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:08,743
[laughs] HEY, SEX SELLS.
THAT'S A FACT OF LIFE.

106
00:05:08,743 --> 00:05:10,875
OH, YEAH.

107
00:05:10,875 --> 00:05:13,704
LISTEN, HER ACTUAL
PITCHING SKILLS--BUSH LEAGUE.

108
00:05:13,704 --> 00:05:16,533
YOU PUT A BAG ON HER,
LISELLE COULDN'T SELL SQUAT.

109
00:05:16,533 --> 00:05:19,362
EVER ASK HER OUT?YEAH.

110
00:05:19,362 --> 00:05:21,582
HOW'D THAT GO FOR YOU?

111
00:05:21,582 --> 00:05:23,888
UH, SHE SAID NO. BOYFRIEND.

112
00:05:23,888 --> 00:05:25,977
WHAT WAS HIS NAME?

113
00:05:25,977 --> 00:05:28,893
UM, UH, JEFF. JEFF SOMEBODY--
MUSICIAN, WANNABE ROCK STAR.

114
00:05:28,893 --> 00:05:30,852
YEAH, SHE WAS
ALWAYS BITCHING ABOUT HIM.

115
00:05:30,852 --> 00:05:32,506
ALWAYS DRAMA WITH THOSE TWO.

116
00:05:34,116 --> 00:05:36,248
BOYFRIEND IS JEFF SPARHAWK.

117
00:05:36,248 --> 00:05:38,599
THE VICTIM HAD A LOFT WITH HIM
SOUTH OF MARKET.

118
00:05:38,599 --> 00:05:41,515
HERE'S THE ADDRESS.JANE AND I WILL LOOK INTO IT.

119
00:05:41,515 --> 00:05:44,082
YOU CHECK
OUT HER FINANCIALS.YOU WANTED TO SEE ME, BOSS?

120
00:05:44,082 --> 00:05:48,652
ACTUALLY, I WANTED TO SEE BOTH
OF YOU. SHUT THE DOOR. SIT DOWN.

121
00:05:57,444 --> 00:05:59,794
YOU KNOW WHAT THIS IS ABOUT.

122
00:05:59,794 --> 00:06:02,884
THE OTHER DAY YOU TOLD ME
YOU WERE INVOLVED

123
00:06:02,884 --> 00:06:06,583
IN A ROMANTIC RELATIONSHIP
WITH EACH OTHER.YES.

124
00:06:06,583 --> 00:06:08,977
DATING WITHIN THE UNIT IS

125
00:06:08,977 --> 00:06:11,893
STRICTLY AGAINST
CBI REGULATIONS.

126
00:06:11,893 --> 00:06:15,766
I WANTED TO TAKE SOME TIME
TO THINK ABOUT HOW TO RESPOND,

127
00:06:15,766 --> 00:06:18,769
BUT I REALIZE
THAT IT'S CAUSING TENSION, SO...

128
00:06:20,815 --> 00:06:23,208
AGENT RIGSBY AND VAN PELT,

129
00:06:23,208 --> 00:06:26,951
ARE YOU INVOLVED IN A PERSONAL
RELATIONSHIP WITH EACH OTHER?

130
00:06:26,951 --> 00:06:29,519
YES.WE ARE.

131
00:06:29,519 --> 00:06:31,042
OKAY, THEN.

132
00:06:31,042 --> 00:06:34,045
AS YOUR SUPERVISOR, I HAVE
TO REPORT THE RELATIONSHIP

133
00:06:34,045 --> 00:06:36,526
TO EMPLOYEE SUPPORT SERVICES.
I'M GONNA DO IT

134
00:06:36,526 --> 00:06:38,876
AS SOON AS
WE CLOSE THIS CASE.

135
00:06:38,876 --> 00:06:41,618
DO YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS?

136
00:06:41,618 --> 00:06:45,187
BUT THEY'LL MAKE ONE OF US
TRANSFER OUT OF THE UNIT.

137
00:06:45,187 --> 00:06:47,189
YES, THEY WILL.

138
00:06:47,189 --> 00:06:49,060
THAT'S THE RULE.
YOU KNEW THAT.

139
00:06:53,804 --> 00:06:55,676
YOU CAN GO NOW.

140
00:07:04,815 --> 00:07:08,210
WHERE THE HELL IS 4-B?

141
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:10,560
[thunder rumbles in distance]I UNDERSTAND YOUR POSITION.

142
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:13,737
THERE'S NO NEED
TO BEAT YOURSELF UP ABOUT IT.WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

143
00:07:13,737 --> 00:07:17,088
WELL, THAT YOU FEEL BAD
ABOUT RIGSBY AND VAN PELT.NO, I DON'T.

144
00:07:17,088 --> 00:07:19,308
WELL,
YOU CAN'T HELP WONDERING

145
00:07:19,308 --> 00:07:22,833
IF THERE'S A HINT OF JEALOUSY
AND RESENTMENT IN YOUR DECISION.EXCUSE ME?

146
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,835
[loud thumping]

147
00:07:24,835 --> 00:07:26,315
AH.

148
00:07:26,315 --> 00:07:29,492
[door squeaks open]

149
00:07:29,492 --> 00:07:32,452
MR. SPARHAWK?[clatter]

150
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:35,672
WE'RE WITH THE CALIFORNIA
BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION.

151
00:07:35,672 --> 00:07:37,065
[pants]

152
00:07:37,065 --> 00:07:39,763
CALIFORNIA WHAT?

153
00:07:39,763 --> 00:07:43,724
WE WANT TO ASK YOU
SOME QUESTIONS ABOUT LISELLE.

154
00:07:43,724 --> 00:07:46,901
YOU WANT TO PUT DOWN
WHAT'S LEFT OF YOUR GUITAR?

155
00:07:46,901 --> 00:07:49,817
YEAH. WHATEVER.

156
00:07:49,817 --> 00:07:51,253
[thud]

157
00:07:51,253 --> 00:07:53,995
I'LL MAKE SOME TEA.

158
00:07:56,563 --> 00:07:58,565
WHY ALL THE DEMOLITION,
JEFF?

159
00:07:58,565 --> 00:08:01,655
I'M SAD. I LIKE
TO DESTROY THINGS WHEN I'M SAD.

160
00:08:01,655 --> 00:08:04,919
WELL, SOME SADNESS,
BUT MOSTLY GUILT,

161
00:08:04,919 --> 00:08:07,356
A DOLLOP OF SELF-PITY,

162
00:08:07,356 --> 00:08:09,924
TINGLE OF EXCITEMENT.

163
00:08:09,924 --> 00:08:13,493
SO YOU'RE A MUSICIAN?

164
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,364
ALL RIGHT.

165
00:08:15,364 --> 00:08:16,800
YOU ANY GOOD?

166
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,759
NO.

167
00:08:18,759 --> 00:08:21,718
YOU'RE OKAY. I COULD TELL
LISELLE WAS A WOMAN OF TASTE.

168
00:08:21,718 --> 00:08:23,851
SHE WOULDN'T HAVE LOVED
A BAD MUSICIAN.

169
00:08:23,851 --> 00:08:25,330
YEAH.

170
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:27,550
I'M GREAT. HUGE.

171
00:08:27,550 --> 00:08:30,727
LAST YEAR I MADE $9,000
FOR MY MUSIC.

172
00:08:30,727 --> 00:08:33,556
WELL, THAT'S $9,000 MORE THAN
VAN GOGH EVER MADE FROM HIS ART.

173
00:08:33,556 --> 00:08:34,949
[chuckles and sniffles]

174
00:08:34,949 --> 00:08:36,994
YEAH,
THINGS WORKED OUT FOR HIM.

175
00:08:36,994 --> 00:08:39,736
OKAY. SO, UM, LISELLE
WAS THE BREADWINNER?

176
00:08:39,736 --> 00:08:42,391
YEAH. HER CUT ON AN ASTON...

177
00:08:42,391 --> 00:08:44,436
[sniffles] COULD KEEP US GOING
FOR A COUPLE MONTHS,

178
00:08:44,436 --> 00:08:47,222
SO I COULD CONCENTRATE
ON MY MUSIC.

179
00:08:47,222 --> 00:08:49,964
SHE DID IT FOR ME.
SHE HATED THAT JOB.

180
00:08:49,964 --> 00:08:51,792
DID THAT EVER CAUSE TENSION
IN YOUR RELATIONSHIP?

181
00:08:51,792 --> 00:08:53,750
SURE.

182
00:08:53,750 --> 00:08:55,839
COUPLES FIGHT.

183
00:08:55,839 --> 00:08:58,059
I DIDN'T LIKE HER WORKING
AT THAT PLACE, BUT...

184
00:08:58,059 --> 00:09:01,149
YOU NEEDED THE MONEY.
IT'S FAIR ENOUGH.

185
00:09:01,149 --> 00:09:04,021
SHE WAS GETTING HIT ON
ALL THE TIME

186
00:09:04,021 --> 00:09:06,981
BY RICH EGOMANIACS, OKAY?

187
00:09:06,981 --> 00:09:09,026
IT'S GONNA MAKE YOU JEALOUS,
RIGHT?

188
00:09:09,026 --> 00:09:11,768
GUYS, UH,
GUYS TRY TO GIVE HER STUFF.WHAT KIND OF STUFF?

189
00:09:11,768 --> 00:09:14,945
YOU KNOW,
UH, JEWELRY, PERFUME,

190
00:09:14,945 --> 00:09:18,819
STUFF LIKE THAT.
LISELLE ALWAYS SENT IT BACK.

191
00:09:18,819 --> 00:09:21,865
WHY?OUT OF RESPECT FOR ME.

192
00:09:21,865 --> 00:09:26,000
OR IF SHE COULDN'T GIVE IT BACK,
SHE GAVE IT AWAY.NOT ALL OF IT.

193
00:09:28,002 --> 00:09:31,701
THIS IS VERY VALUABLE.

194
00:09:31,701 --> 00:09:35,531
LISELLE SAID IT WAS
TOO VALUABLE TO GET RID OF.

195
00:09:35,531 --> 00:09:38,578
SHE SAID WE'D USE IT TO, UH,
PAY FOR OUR WEDDING.

196
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:41,668
WHO GAVE HER THE PRINT?

197
00:09:41,668 --> 00:09:45,019
[crying] I'VE DONE BAD,
STUPID THINGS.

198
00:09:45,019 --> 00:09:47,630
I NEVER DESERVED HER.

199
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,589
AND NOW SHE'S GONE. GOD.

200
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,199
OH, STOP.

201
00:09:51,199 --> 00:09:53,027
SELF-PITY'LL KILL YOU.

202
00:09:54,855 --> 00:09:57,814
TAKE IT FROM SOMEONE THAT KNOWS.

203
00:09:57,814 --> 00:10:00,077
JEFF SPARHAWK
HAS NO ALIBI.

204
00:10:00,077 --> 00:10:02,558
YOU CAN DISPENSE
WITH THE COP TALK, LISBON.

205
00:10:02,558 --> 00:10:05,517
YOU CAN TELL ME
WHAT'S BOTHERING YOU.NOTHING'S BOTHERING ME.

206
00:10:05,517 --> 00:10:07,955
OKAY.NOTHING IS BOTHERING ME.

207
00:10:07,955 --> 00:10:10,218
MESSAGE RECEIVED.GOOD.

208
00:10:10,218 --> 00:10:12,307
SPARHAWK--NO ALIBI, YEAH?

209
00:10:12,307 --> 00:10:13,961
MM.

210
00:10:13,961 --> 00:10:16,006
[car doors close][Lisbon] BY THE WAY,

211
00:10:16,006 --> 00:10:17,965
WHAT DO YOU MEAN
I'M JEALOUS AND RESENTFUL?

212
00:10:17,965 --> 00:10:19,619
IT WAS NONSENSE.

213
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:22,099
[Patrick] YET YOU RECALL
MY EXACT WORDS.

214
00:10:22,099 --> 00:10:25,712
THERE'S NO SHAME IN IT. I FEEL
THAT WAY, TOO, SOMETIMES.

215
00:10:25,712 --> 00:10:28,671
WHY DOES EVERYONE ELSE
GET TO HAVE A NORMAL LIFE?

216
00:10:28,671 --> 00:10:30,194
MY LIFE IS FINE.

217
00:10:30,194 --> 00:10:32,893
NORMALLY YOU RISE ABOVE
SUCH CRAVEN EMOTIONS,

218
00:10:32,893 --> 00:10:35,286
BUT IN THIS CASE,
YOUR HANDS WERE TIED.

219
00:10:35,286 --> 00:10:37,288
IT'S THE RULES.
YOU'RE FORCED TO DO

220
00:10:37,288 --> 00:10:40,291
WHAT YOUR WORST SELF IS
TELLING YOU TO DO ANYWAY.

221
00:10:40,291 --> 00:10:42,380
HENCE, YOUR TENSION HEADACHE.

222
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:45,253
I DON'T...

223
00:10:45,253 --> 00:10:47,037
ALL RIGHT.

224
00:10:47,037 --> 00:10:49,605
I-I DO HAVE A HEADACHE,
BUT THAT'S A COINCIDENCE.

225
00:10:49,605 --> 00:10:51,172
NAH.

226
00:10:51,172 --> 00:10:53,174
EITHER I OBEY THE RULES

227
00:10:53,174 --> 00:10:55,655
OR I RISK TAKING BIG HEAT
FOR IGNORING THEM.

228
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:59,267
THIS IS ON VAN PELT
AND RIGSBY, NOT ME.WHATEVER YOU SAY.

229
00:10:59,267 --> 00:11:01,878
[cell phone rings]LISBON.

230
00:11:01,878 --> 00:11:04,489
[Van Pelt] Hey, I found
something on that print.

231
00:11:04,489 --> 00:11:07,318
IT SOLD AT AUCTION
IN SAN FRANCISCO LAST YEAR,

232
00:11:07,318 --> 00:11:10,365
PURCHASED BY WALTER MASHBURN
FOR 30 GRAND.

233
00:11:10,365 --> 00:11:12,759
MASHBURN. SOUNDS FAMILIAR.
[mouths word]

234
00:11:12,759 --> 00:11:14,717
HE FOUNDED MASHBURN AVIONICS,

235
00:11:14,717 --> 00:11:16,719
SOLD IT TEN YEARS AGO
FOR BILLIONS.

236
00:11:16,719 --> 00:11:18,678
HE WAS ALSO LISELLE DOUGLAS'
LAST APPOINTMENT

237
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:20,244
THE DAY SHE DIED.

238
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:26,686
DID YOU NOTICE THE BADGE,
OR SHOULD I SHOW YOU AGAIN?

239
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:30,124
I'M SO SORRY, BUT I CAN'T SAY
IF MR. MASHBURN IS HERE OR NOT.

240
00:11:30,124 --> 00:11:33,475
WE'RE A PRIVATE CLUB, AND OUR
MEMBERS TREASURE THEIR PRIVACY.

241
00:11:33,475 --> 00:11:35,346
[whispers] DON'T WORRY.
I'LL FIND HIM.

242
00:11:35,346 --> 00:11:38,349
[indistinct conversations]

243
00:11:38,349 --> 00:11:40,787
W--EXCUSE ME, SIR.

244
00:11:44,921 --> 00:11:47,837
WELL, HELLO THERE.

245
00:11:47,837 --> 00:11:49,665
THE DECK, CORNER TABLE?

246
00:11:49,665 --> 00:11:51,928
HUH?

247
00:11:51,928 --> 00:11:54,061
OH, YOU MUST BE NEW.
WALTER MASHBURN.

248
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,848
I LIKED LISELLE.

249
00:11:58,848 --> 00:12:00,763
SMART WOMAN. DAMN SHAME.

250
00:12:00,763 --> 00:12:03,026
AND YOU GAVE HER
AN EXPENSIVE GIFT.

251
00:12:03,026 --> 00:12:06,029
YES.WERE YOU SLEEPING WITH HER?

252
00:12:06,029 --> 00:12:09,424
[chuckles] IF I SLEPT
WITH EVERYONE I GAVE GIFTS TO,

253
00:12:09,424 --> 00:12:11,861
I WOULDN'T GET
ANY WORK DONE...

254
00:12:11,861 --> 00:12:16,779
OR ANY SLEEP,
FOR THAT MATTER.BUT YOU PROPOSITIONED HER,
AND SHE SAID NO.

255
00:12:16,779 --> 00:12:18,215
[chuckles]

256
00:12:18,215 --> 00:12:19,739
PERCEPTIVE.

257
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:24,482
YOU'RE A PSYCHIC,
AREN'T YOU?

258
00:12:24,482 --> 00:12:27,050
WHAT MAKES YOU SAY THAT?

259
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:29,009
YOU HAVE THIS CHARLATAN AIR
ABOUT YOU.

260
00:12:29,009 --> 00:12:30,314
[chuckles]

261
00:12:30,314 --> 00:12:32,621
MY SECOND...

262
00:12:32,621 --> 00:12:35,929
NO, MY THIRD WIFE WAS INTO
ALL THAT MYSTICAL GOOP.

263
00:12:35,929 --> 00:12:39,193
MM-HMM.YOU LEARN
TO RECOGNIZE THE TYPE.

264
00:12:39,193 --> 00:12:41,848
HOW MANY WIVES HAVE YOU HAD?

265
00:12:41,848 --> 00:12:43,850
[chuckles]
ENOUGH TO KNOW BETTER.

266
00:12:43,850 --> 00:12:45,765
BUT I'M CURRENTLY
UNATTACHED.

267
00:12:48,985 --> 00:12:52,989
SO WERE YOU SLEEPING
WITH LISELLE OR NOT?

268
00:12:52,989 --> 00:12:55,600
NOT.

269
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,733
THAT PRINT WAS A REWARD

270
00:12:57,733 --> 00:13:00,910
FOR FINDING ME AN AUSTIN HEALEY
2-SEATER FROM 1960.

271
00:13:00,910 --> 00:13:03,521
THERE WAS
ONLY A FEW HUNDRED MADE.MM-HMM.

272
00:13:03,521 --> 00:13:06,829
SHE EARNED THAT GIFT.AND THE APPOINTMENT YOU HAD
WITH HER THE DAY SHE DIED?

273
00:13:06,829 --> 00:13:09,789
TO PICK THE CAR UP.
DO YOU WANT TO SEE IT?NO, THANKS.

274
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,834
I'D LOVE TO.

275
00:13:11,834 --> 00:13:15,011
YOU HAVE A DAMAGED INTENSITY
THAT'S QUITE ATTRACTIVE.

276
00:13:15,011 --> 00:13:16,839
MM. YEAH.

277
00:13:16,839 --> 00:13:20,843
LET ME BUY YOU
A DRINK SOMETIME.I LIVE IN SACRAMENTO.

278
00:13:20,843 --> 00:13:23,759
I HAVE A JET.OH, YOU'RE VERY GOOD.
VERY GOOD.

279
00:13:23,759 --> 00:13:26,980
I HAVE ONE QUESTION--
UH, DID YOU KILL LISELLE?

280
00:13:28,895 --> 00:13:31,332
HMM?

281
00:13:31,332 --> 00:13:34,901
JAKE, CHECK, PLEASE.

282
00:13:34,901 --> 00:13:37,033
LET ME SHOW YOU FOLKS
SOMETHING.

283
00:13:37,033 --> 00:13:41,037
[Walter] SMUGGLERS CALL 'EM
GO-FAST BOATS--SAYS IT ALL.

284
00:13:41,037 --> 00:13:43,866
NOTHING LIKE FLYING
ACROSS THE OCEAN AT 80 KNOTS

285
00:13:43,866 --> 00:13:45,520
TO GET THE BLOOD GOING.

286
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,739
WOULD YOU LIKE
TO COME FOR A RIDE?

287
00:13:47,739 --> 00:13:50,046
WE GET IT.
YOU'RE AN ENERGETIC MAN.

288
00:13:50,046 --> 00:13:52,832
YOU LIKE DANGER.
SO WHY BRING US HERE?

289
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:54,790
I HAVE NO LOVE FOR DANGER.

290
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:57,837
NOTHING'S DANGEROUS
IF YOU THINK AHEAD.

291
00:13:57,837 --> 00:14:00,448
IF YOU PLAN IT RIGHT,
YOU CAN GET AWAY WITH...

292
00:14:00,448 --> 00:14:03,668
WELL, I WAS GONNA SAY YOU CAN
GET AWAY WITH MURDER, BUT...

293
00:14:03,668 --> 00:14:06,976
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

294
00:14:06,976 --> 00:14:08,760
OKAY. SO...

295
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:12,155
WHAT'S THE POINT IN SHOWING US
YOUR FANCY TOY HERE?

296
00:14:12,155 --> 00:14:15,942
THIS IS HOW I LIVE MY LIFE.
I HAVE A CASTLE IN SCOTLAND,

297
00:14:15,942 --> 00:14:18,901
A COMPOUND ON THE WATERFRONT
IN MARIN.

298
00:14:18,901 --> 00:14:21,861
IF I KILLED LISELLE,
WOULD I STUFF HER IN THE TRUNK

299
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:25,299
LIKE SOME LOW-RENT THUG?HOW WOULD YOU HAVE DONE IT?

300
00:14:25,299 --> 00:14:27,344
SHE WOULD HAVE
JUST DISAPPEARED,

301
00:14:27,344 --> 00:14:30,826
LIKE SMOKE,
LIKE SHE WAS NEVER THERE.

302
00:14:30,826 --> 00:14:33,873
YOU ENJOY BEING
A MURDER SUSPECT, DON'T YOU?

303
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:36,484
AM I? A SUSPECT?

304
00:14:36,484 --> 00:14:39,139
OF COURSE. IT COULD BE
YOU'RE A SOCIOPATH,

305
00:14:39,139 --> 00:14:41,968
OR IT COULD BE THAT KILLING IS
A THRILL THAT YOU CAN'T BUY.

306
00:14:43,795 --> 00:14:46,320
NOT A LOT EXCITES YOU ANYMORE,
DOES IT, WALTER?

307
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:50,019
PATRICK, IF YOU REALLY THINK
I KILLED LISELLE,

308
00:14:50,019 --> 00:14:53,718
THERE'S ONLY ONE THING
FOR YOU TO DO.

309
00:14:53,718 --> 00:14:56,591
TRY AND CATCH ME.[boat engine starts]

310
00:15:09,604 --> 00:15:11,432
THAT COULD BE YOU.

311
00:15:16,089 --> 00:15:19,048
MASHBURN'S GOT ZERO PRIORS,
BUT HE'S BEEN INVESTIGATED

312
00:15:19,048 --> 00:15:22,530
FOR SEVERAL
SHADY BUSINESS DEALS.BUT THEY NEVER FOUND
ANYTHING.

313
00:15:22,530 --> 00:15:25,881
LEGIT BUSINESS GENIUS,
IT SAYS HERE.HE THINKS HE'S A GENIUS.
HE'S A PIRATE THAT GOT LUCKY.

314
00:15:25,881 --> 00:15:29,667
HE'S GOTTEN EVERYTHING HE WANTED
SINCE HE WAS 30 YEARS OLD.EXCEPT YOU.

315
00:15:29,667 --> 00:15:31,626
WAIT. WALTER MASHBURN
ASKED YOU OUT?

316
00:15:31,626 --> 00:15:33,323
NO.

317
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:37,675
WELL, SORT OF.WOW.

318
00:15:37,675 --> 00:15:39,895
PERSONALLY, I THOUGHT
SHE SHOULD HAVE GONE FOR IT.

319
00:15:39,895 --> 00:15:42,463
A LITTLE EMPTY GLAMOUR
WOULD HAVE BEEN GOOD FOR HER.

320
00:15:42,463 --> 00:15:45,466
BUT, NO, NOT OUR LISBON.RIGSBY, WHY DON'T YOU GO

321
00:15:45,466 --> 00:15:48,469
AND TALK TO HIS ALIBI,
THE SWIMSUIT MODEL?

322
00:15:48,469 --> 00:15:51,994
OH, SURE, YEAH, THE SWIMSUIT
MODEL. UH, NO PROBLEM.

323
00:15:51,994 --> 00:15:53,604
THE ALIBI WILL BE SOLID,
WHETHER HE DID IT OR NOT.

324
00:15:53,604 --> 00:15:55,824
CHECK ANYWAY.I GOT SOMETHING.

325
00:15:55,824 --> 00:15:58,392
IT SEEMS WESTHOFF,
THE BOSS AT ZENITH MOTORS,

326
00:15:58,392 --> 00:16:00,568
REPORTED A FERRARI DISAPPEARED
FROM THEIR SERVICE DEPARTMENT

327
00:16:00,568 --> 00:16:03,484
THE NIGHT OF THE MURDER.
BUT AN HOUR LATER,

328
00:16:03,484 --> 00:16:06,574
WESTHOFF CALLED THE SHERIFF BACK
AND SAID NEVER MIND.SO HE FOUND THE CAR?

329
00:16:06,574 --> 00:16:09,403
[Cho] DIDN'T SAY.WE NEED TO FIND OUT.
I GOT THE AUTOPSY REPORT.

330
00:16:09,403 --> 00:16:11,448
LISELLE DIED
OF MAJOR HEAD TRAUMA

331
00:16:11,448 --> 00:16:13,494
CAUSED BY FORCEFUL CONTACT
WITH THE PAVEMENT.

332
00:16:13,494 --> 00:16:15,844
THAT PUT TOGETHER WITH
SKIN ABRASIONS, BONE FRACTURES--

333
00:16:15,844 --> 00:16:18,803
SHE WAS HIT BY A CAR.WELL, IF A CAR IS
THE MURDER WEAPON,

334
00:16:18,803 --> 00:16:20,936
IT'LL HAVE TRACE EVIDENCE
ON IT--BLOOD, D.N.A.--

335
00:16:20,936 --> 00:16:23,069
EVEN IF THE KILLER WASHED IT.

336
00:16:23,069 --> 00:16:25,680
TALK TO WESTHOFF. D.N.A.
EVIDENCE DOESN'T LAST FOREVER.OKAY.

337
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:28,465
[whistles] WHOO.

338
00:16:29,858 --> 00:16:32,469
I'M OUT SICK TWO DAYS,

339
00:16:32,469 --> 00:16:36,430
AND YOU GIVE THE TARLEN ACCOUNT
TO LEGLER?YOU'VE BEEN SICK ON AND OFF
FOR A MONTH.

340
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:39,476
IT'S NOT MY FAULT
I GOT A STOMACH BUG.HEY, NO FREE RIDES.

341
00:16:39,476 --> 00:16:42,436
YOU EAT WHAT YOU KILL HERE--
THAT'S RULE NUMBER ONE.DON'T TELL ME ABOUT RULES,
YOU SON OF A BITCH.

342
00:16:42,436 --> 00:16:44,655
THIS IS ME TALKING.OH, YOU?

343
00:16:44,655 --> 00:16:47,571
YEAH.YOU NEED TO REMEMBER WHICH ONE
OF US HERE IS THE MAN.

344
00:16:47,571 --> 00:16:50,574
[knock on door]HEY, GUYS.
ARE WE INTERRUPTING SOMETHING?

345
00:16:53,490 --> 00:16:55,927
MANAGEMENT SEMINAR.

346
00:16:55,927 --> 00:16:57,625
TRADITIONALLY
IN THESE DOMINANCE DISPLAYS,

347
00:16:57,625 --> 00:17:01,237
IT'S CUSTOMARY TO, UH,
BARE ONE'S CANINES.

348
00:17:03,239 --> 00:17:07,156
SOME SPECIES GO SO FAR AS
EXPOSING THEIR GENITALS. YEAH?

349
00:17:07,156 --> 00:17:11,073
1986 FERRARI TESTAROSSA--
BELONGS TO AN ALEXA LANDAU,

350
00:17:11,073 --> 00:17:14,903
AND IT DISAPPEARED FROM YOUR
SERVICE DEPARTMENT. WHERE IS IT?I DON'T KNOW.

351
00:17:14,903 --> 00:17:19,429
THEN WHY'D YOU TELL THE COPS
"NEVER MIND"?'CAUSE I TOLD HIM THE OWNER'S
HUSBAND MAY HAVE TAKEN THE CAR.

352
00:17:19,429 --> 00:17:23,346
WE TRY NOT TO CALL THE POLICE
ON OUR CLIENTS.HE STOLE
HIS OWN WIFE'S CAR?

353
00:17:23,346 --> 00:17:25,392
YEAH,
LANDAUS ARE SPLITTING UP.

354
00:17:25,392 --> 00:17:28,482
YOU KNOW, RICH PEOPLE AND THEIR
FRICKIN' SOAP OPERA LIVES.

355
00:17:28,482 --> 00:17:31,441
APPARENTLY, THE HUSBAND TOOK
THE CAR TO VEGAS, PARTIED HARD,

356
00:17:31,441 --> 00:17:35,010
LEFT THE CAR A MESS.
NOW ALEXA'S PISSED.AND BEFORE SHE JETS OFF
TO MILAN,

357
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:38,579
SHE BRINGS IT IN
TO BE DETAILED,

358
00:17:38,579 --> 00:17:41,930
SPECIFICALLY TELLS KINSEY NOT
TO LET HER PIG HUSBAND NEAR IT.

359
00:17:41,930 --> 00:17:45,107
HE TELLS ME THIS LATER.[Cho] AND YOU THINK THE HUSBAND
DIDN'T TAKE NO FOR AN ANSWER?

360
00:17:45,107 --> 00:17:48,284
NOAH LANDAU'S
A BIG RECORD PRODUCER,

361
00:17:48,284 --> 00:17:51,722
NOT REALLY KNOWN FOR HIS IMPULSE
CONTROL. AND HE LOVES THAT CAR.NOAH LANDAU WAS
AT THE COCKTAIL PARTY

362
00:17:51,722 --> 00:17:54,421
WHEN LISELLE'S BODY WAS
DISCOVERED. I'LL TALK TO LISBON.

363
00:17:54,421 --> 00:17:58,033
MM. "RICH PEOPLE AND THEIR
FRICKIN' SOAP OPERA LIVES."

364
00:17:58,033 --> 00:18:01,602
YOU DON'T REALLY LIKE RICH
PEOPLE MUCH, DO YOU, KINSEY?ARE YOU KIDDING?
I LOVE 'EM.

365
00:18:01,602 --> 00:18:05,214
I'M ON THE WAY UP, MY FRIEND.
RICH PEOPLE ARE TAKING ME THERE.

366
00:18:05,214 --> 00:18:07,216
WELL, SOMEDAY,
BUT IN THE MEANTIME,

367
00:18:07,216 --> 00:18:09,871
LANDAU IS DINING AT SOME
LAVISH RESTAURANT IN LAS VEGAS.

368
00:18:09,871 --> 00:18:11,481
SITTING ACROSS THE TABLE

369
00:18:11,481 --> 00:18:13,483
FROM HIM IS A WOMAN
PROBABLY HALF HIS AGE

370
00:18:13,483 --> 00:18:16,007
THAT'S LAUGHING
AT EVERY ONE OF HIS JOKES.

371
00:18:16,007 --> 00:18:19,402
AND YOU'RE STUCK HERE WITH THIS
GUY, REHEATING... BEEF SOUP?

372
00:18:19,402 --> 00:18:23,537
BEEF--BEEF BARLEY.
DO YOU MIND?SURE.

373
00:18:23,537 --> 00:18:26,757
WOULD YOU SAY
YOU HAVE FOOD ISSUES?

374
00:18:26,757 --> 00:18:29,760
YOU DON'T HAVE TO ANSWER THAT.
WERE YOU AN ORPHAN?

375
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:32,546
A LOT OF THIEVES AROUND HERE.

376
00:18:32,546 --> 00:18:35,505
OH, LIKE I'M GONNA STEAL
YOUR LUNCH.WELL, SOMEONE DID.

377
00:18:35,505 --> 00:18:37,986
YEAH, JUST THE OTHER DAY.
HOW LOW IS THAT?

378
00:18:37,986 --> 00:18:40,902
BEEF BARLEY?YEAH.

379
00:18:40,902 --> 00:18:42,512
BEEF--

380
00:18:42,512 --> 00:18:45,341
IT'S NOT REALLY
A POPULAR SOUP MEAT, IS IT?

381
00:18:45,341 --> 00:18:47,952
EACH HIS OWN.

382
00:18:47,952 --> 00:18:49,606
YEAH, I GUESS.

383
00:18:49,606 --> 00:18:52,566
[Van Pelt] SO HE KILLED HER
WHILE STEALING HIS OWN CAR?

384
00:18:52,566 --> 00:18:54,742
[Rigsby] THAT'S THE THEORY.
LOOK, GRACE,

385
00:18:54,742 --> 00:18:57,136
I JUST WANNA LET YOU KNOW
I'M NOT WORRIED

386
00:18:57,136 --> 00:19:00,095
ABOUT LISBON REPORTING US. WE'LL
MAKE IT WORK, WHATEVER HAPPENS.I KNOW WE WILL.

387
00:19:00,095 --> 00:19:02,141
IF WORSE COMES TO WORSE,

388
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:05,187
THEY PROBABLY WOULDN'T TRANSFER
YOU OUT OF THE CENTRAL VALLEY.

389
00:19:05,187 --> 00:19:08,147
L.A. OR SOMETHING LIKE THAT
IS REALLY UNLIKELY.WELL, YOU'RE ASSUMING
I'M THE ONE TO BE TRANSFERRED?

390
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:11,062
YEAH, I'VE BEEN HERE
ALMOST FIVE YEARS, SO SENIORITY,

391
00:19:11,062 --> 00:19:14,065
PLUS, THIS IS MY CAREER,
YOU KNOW?IT'S MY CAREER, TOO, WAYNE.

392
00:19:14,065 --> 00:19:16,242
NO,
I DIDN'T MEAN IT THAT WAY.

393
00:19:16,242 --> 00:19:19,070
OBVIOUSLY, YOU CAN HAVE
A CAREER AS WELL.THANKS FOR YOUR PERMISSION.

394
00:19:22,465 --> 00:19:25,555
WHY WOULD I STEAL
MY OWN CAR?OH, IT WAS YOUR WIFE'S CAR,
MR. LANDAU,

395
00:19:25,555 --> 00:19:27,992
YOUR, UH, ESTRANGED WIFE?

396
00:19:27,992 --> 00:19:31,213
YEAH, WELL, WE'RE UH--
WHAT DO YOU CALL--RECONCILING.

397
00:19:31,213 --> 00:19:32,954
OH? CONGRATULATIONS.

398
00:19:32,954 --> 00:19:34,608
THAT'S NICE.

399
00:19:34,608 --> 00:19:38,699
SO THE TRIP TO VEGAS
WAS A LAST HURRAH?

400
00:19:38,699 --> 00:19:42,398
YES, WE KNOW ABOUT IT.
WE KNOW EVERYTHING, MR. LANDAU.

401
00:19:42,398 --> 00:19:45,314
LISELLE DOUGLAS SOLD YOUR WIFE
THAT CAR. YOU KNOW HER?

402
00:19:45,314 --> 00:19:48,404
REALLY?
LISELLE SOLD METHAT CAR.

403
00:19:48,404 --> 00:19:51,407
'86 TESTAROSSA--
FRICKIN' CLASSIC.

404
00:19:51,407 --> 00:19:54,802
YOU THINK ALEXA EVEN CARED?
SHE CAN'T EVEN DRIVE STICK.

405
00:19:54,802 --> 00:19:57,413
SO YOU TOOK WHAT WAS YOURS.
THAT'S UNDERSTANDABLE.

406
00:19:57,413 --> 00:19:59,110
YOU KNOW WHAT?

407
00:19:59,110 --> 00:20:02,026
YOU SHOULD LEAVE.YOU KILLED HER, DIDN'T YOU?

408
00:20:02,026 --> 00:20:06,248
RAN LISELLE DOWN WHEN SHE
CAUGHT YOU TAKING THE CAR.WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.
WAIT A SECOND. WAIT A SECOND.

409
00:20:06,248 --> 00:20:09,599
THAT'S HOW SHE DIED?WELL, MAYBE YOU DIDN'T SEE HER
UNTIL IT WAS TOO LATE.

410
00:20:09,599 --> 00:20:13,603
IT WAS DARK. HELP YOURSELF,
MR. LANDAU. TELL US YOUR SIDE.

411
00:20:13,603 --> 00:20:15,518
[whispers] WOW.

412
00:20:15,518 --> 00:20:17,346
[normal voice] OH, MAN,
IT'S NOT LIKE THAT.

413
00:20:17,346 --> 00:20:20,436
IT'S NOT LIKE THAT. LOOK...

414
00:20:20,436 --> 00:20:24,005
[sighs] WHEN I GOT BACK
FROM VEGAS,

415
00:20:24,005 --> 00:20:25,398
I, UH,

416
00:20:25,398 --> 00:20:29,967
I-I FORGOT SOME, UH,
STUFF IN MY CAR.

417
00:20:29,967 --> 00:20:31,404
DRUGS?

418
00:20:31,404 --> 00:20:34,145
NO. YEAH, DRUGS. WHAT ELSE?

419
00:20:34,145 --> 00:20:36,583
ALEXA AND I--

420
00:20:36,583 --> 00:20:38,802
WE'RE WORKING OUT
CUSTODY OF OUR SON.

421
00:20:38,802 --> 00:20:43,111
SO YOU COULD SEE HOW A DRUG BUST
COULD LOOK BAD.WELL, A PLACE LIKE ZENITH

422
00:20:43,111 --> 00:20:47,463
WOULD NEVER CALL THE POLICE
ON A CLIENT.OF COURSE NOT. THEY'D POLITELY
LEAVE IT IN THE GLOVE BOX,

423
00:20:47,463 --> 00:20:50,466
WHERE ALEXA WOULD FIND IT
AND HAVE ME THROWN IN PRISON.

424
00:20:50,466 --> 00:20:53,295
THAT'S WHY I HAD TO GET THE CAR
BEFORE SHE FOUND THE DOPE.

425
00:20:53,295 --> 00:20:55,558
SO YOU STOLE IT.

426
00:20:55,558 --> 00:20:58,648
UH, NO. I ASKED SOMEONE
TO DO ME A FAVOR.

427
00:20:58,648 --> 00:21:01,172
AND THEN I WAS PARTYING,
I LOST MY PHONE,

428
00:21:01,172 --> 00:21:03,392
I CAN'T GET AHOLD OF THE GUY.

429
00:21:03,392 --> 00:21:05,612
THAT'S WHY I WENT
TO THAT STUPID COCKTAIL PARTY,

430
00:21:05,612 --> 00:21:07,440
TO TRY TO HOOK UP WITH HIM.HE'S A SALESMAN?

431
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,442
NO, NO.
IT'S LISELLE'S BOYFRIEND.

432
00:21:09,442 --> 00:21:13,272
HIS NAME IS JEFF SPARHAWK.
HE'S GOT THE CAR.

433
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:16,318
JUMPED AT THE CHANCE
TO GET CLOSE TO ME, SO I WAS...

434
00:21:18,538 --> 00:21:22,542
SHOULD HAVE JUST ASKED HIM
TO KILL MY WIFE.

435
00:21:22,542 --> 00:21:25,458
THAT'S A JOKE. [laughs]

436
00:21:27,155 --> 00:21:29,462
YOU GUYS, MAN.

437
00:21:29,462 --> 00:21:31,290
OOH.

438
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:34,989
[hip-hop music playing]

439
00:21:34,989 --> 00:21:36,556
[Patrick] WHOA!

440
00:21:36,556 --> 00:21:38,558
EXCUSE ME. MR. JANE.

441
00:21:38,558 --> 00:21:40,690
[loudly] WHAT? OH, SORRY.

442
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:43,127
IF YOU COULD JUST--
RIGHT OVER HERE.[music stops, car turns off]

443
00:21:43,127 --> 00:21:47,088
I'M SORRY, MR. JANE. YOU CANNOT
HANG OUT IN THE MERCHANDISE.

444
00:21:47,088 --> 00:21:50,874
OH. OKAY. UH, WELL, WHAT WE NEED
THEN IS A TEST DRIVE.

445
00:21:50,874 --> 00:21:53,268
DOWN TO THE BEACH
WOULD BE GOOD.

446
00:21:53,268 --> 00:21:55,966
YOU'RE LOOKING TO BUY?ABSOLUTELY.
WELL, NOT ME, BUT, UH--

447
00:21:55,966 --> 00:21:58,404
I DON'T REALLY CARE
FOR THIS KIND OF OSTENTATION,

448
00:21:58,404 --> 00:22:00,623
BUT CHO LIKES
WHAT YOU'RE COOKING.

449
00:22:00,623 --> 00:22:04,279
DO YOU THINK YOU COULD SHOW US
AROUND THE LOT?YOU KNOW, I'M SO SORRY.

450
00:22:04,279 --> 00:22:07,630
[cell phone ringing]OUR INVENTORY STARTS IN
THE LOW SIX FIGURES, SO I NEED

451
00:22:07,630 --> 00:22:09,632
A BANK STATEMENT BEFORE
I CAN BOOK AN APPOINTMENT.

452
00:22:09,632 --> 00:22:11,591
OTHERWISE WE WOULD BE INUNDATED
WITH REQUESTS. YOU UNDERSTAND.

453
00:22:11,591 --> 00:22:13,636
YEAH, OF COURSE.

454
00:22:13,636 --> 00:22:17,553
UH, YOU'D MAKE AN EXCEPTION
FOR A FRIEND, WOULDN'T YOU?NO.

455
00:22:17,553 --> 00:22:19,207
OH. OKAY.

456
00:22:19,207 --> 00:22:22,210
HEY. WE GOT A LEAD ON SPARHAWK
AND THE MISSING FERRARI.

457
00:22:22,210 --> 00:22:24,212
GOTTA GO.UH, COULD YOU DO ME A FAVOR?

458
00:22:24,212 --> 00:22:27,476
COULD YOU DROP ME SOMEPLACE
ON THE WAY?SURE.

459
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:33,526
[pole whirring]

460
00:22:33,526 --> 00:22:36,398
[boat engine rumbling]

461
00:22:40,184 --> 00:22:43,536
PATRICK.

462
00:22:43,536 --> 00:22:45,842
AHOY!

463
00:22:49,672 --> 00:22:52,545
UNEXPECTED PLEASURE.

464
00:22:52,545 --> 00:22:54,329
WHAT BRINGS YOU HERE?

465
00:22:54,329 --> 00:22:55,678
FISHING.

466
00:22:55,678 --> 00:22:57,245
FOR WHAT?

467
00:22:57,245 --> 00:22:59,073
WHATEVER BITES.

468
00:22:59,073 --> 00:23:02,032
YOU'RE NOT
ON STAKEOUT THEN?

469
00:23:02,032 --> 00:23:05,296
WHAT'S A STAKEOUT?

470
00:23:05,296 --> 00:23:09,213
[siren wails]

471
00:23:09,213 --> 00:23:10,650
THERE'S OUR CAR.

472
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,434
WHERE'S SPARHAWK?

473
00:23:12,434 --> 00:23:15,437
I CAN'T BELIEVE HE COULD WALK
AWAY FROM SOMETHING LIKE THIS

474
00:23:15,437 --> 00:23:18,788
IN ONE PIECE.THAT'S BLOOD ON THE AIR BAG.
HE WAS IN IT, ALL RIGHT.

475
00:23:18,788 --> 00:23:20,442
NO BRAKE MARKS.

476
00:23:20,442 --> 00:23:24,751
HE RAN DIRECTLY
INTO THE POLE.[sirens wailing]

477
00:23:24,751 --> 00:23:28,363
[man] PUT THE SWORD
DOWN NOW.[Jeff] COME ON. COME AND GET ME!

478
00:23:28,363 --> 00:23:30,800
[man] WATCH OUT. WATCH OUT.COME ON, YOU BASTARDS!
COME AND TAKE ME.

479
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:32,976
PUT IT DOWN! PUT IT DOWN.

480
00:23:32,976 --> 00:23:35,501
GO AHEAD AND MAKE ME!

481
00:23:35,501 --> 00:23:37,416
[panting]

482
00:23:40,462 --> 00:23:43,857
DON'T SHOOT HIM
UNLESS HE GOES AT ME FOR REAL.

483
00:23:43,857 --> 00:23:45,467
I DON'T KNOW, BOSS.

484
00:23:45,467 --> 00:23:47,295
BOSS...

485
00:23:56,478 --> 00:23:57,653
JEFF...

486
00:24:00,395 --> 00:24:02,441
WE NEED TO TALK.

487
00:24:08,403 --> 00:24:10,013
JEFF...

488
00:24:10,013 --> 00:24:13,190
PUT THAT THING DOWN NOW.

489
00:24:13,190 --> 00:24:16,019
MAKE ME. [grunts]
GO AHEAD AND MAKE ME!

490
00:24:16,019 --> 00:24:18,674
NOBODY'S GONNA SHOOT YOU,
JEFF...

491
00:24:20,633 --> 00:24:22,939
NO MATTER HOW BADLY
YOU WANT THEM TO.

492
00:24:32,209 --> 00:24:35,125
I KILLED HER.

493
00:24:35,125 --> 00:24:36,562
I KILLED LISELLE.

494
00:24:36,562 --> 00:24:38,607
THEN LET'S TALK ABOUT IT.

495
00:24:38,607 --> 00:24:42,132
LET US HELP YOU, JEFF.

496
00:24:42,132 --> 00:24:44,352
PUT DOWN THE WEAPON.

497
00:24:49,879 --> 00:24:52,839
STAND DOWN.[loud clatter]

498
00:24:54,493 --> 00:24:57,191
YOU'RE UNDER ARREST, JEFF.

499
00:24:57,191 --> 00:24:59,193
WE'RE GONNA TAKE YOU
TO A DOCTOR,

500
00:24:59,193 --> 00:25:01,151
HAVE HIM CHECK YOU OUT.

501
00:25:01,151 --> 00:25:02,588
[handcuffs click]

502
00:25:02,588 --> 00:25:05,547
IS THIS IT? IS THIS
HOW YOU WORK YOUR MAGIC?

503
00:25:05,547 --> 00:25:08,550
WHAT MAGIC'S THAT? OH.

504
00:25:08,550 --> 00:25:10,552
CHECK OUT
THIS LITTLE PUPPY.

505
00:25:10,552 --> 00:25:13,294
THAT'S A KEEPER. [blows]

506
00:25:13,294 --> 00:25:16,253
YOU THINK I DIDN'T
CHECK YOU OUT?

507
00:25:16,253 --> 00:25:17,907
WHAT'D YOU FIND?

508
00:25:17,907 --> 00:25:19,909
PSYCHIC,
JUST AS I CALLED IT.

509
00:25:19,909 --> 00:25:21,911
AH, NO SUCH THING
AS PSYCHICS.

510
00:25:21,911 --> 00:25:25,045
OH, I KNOW. YOU'RE A CHARLATAN,
AS I SAID.

511
00:25:25,045 --> 00:25:27,395
YOU LOST YOUR WIFE AND KID
TO A SERIAL KILLER--

512
00:25:27,395 --> 00:25:29,049
YOUR FAULT, YOU THINK--

513
00:25:29,049 --> 00:25:31,704
AND NOW YOU'RE ON THIS
HOPELESS QUEST FOR REDEMPTION,

514
00:25:31,704 --> 00:25:33,967
BATTLING EVIL AND INJUSTICE,
RIGHT?

515
00:25:33,967 --> 00:25:36,230
[clicks tongue]
CLOSE ENOUGH.

516
00:25:36,230 --> 00:25:39,233
YOU PLAY MIND GAMES WITH PEOPLE,
YOU SIZE UP THEIR WEAKNESSES

517
00:25:39,233 --> 00:25:42,715
AND THEN YOU GIVE THEM THE ROPE
TO HANG THEMSELVES.OH, YOU MAKE IT SOUND SO COOL.

518
00:25:42,715 --> 00:25:45,065
AND AS FOR YOUR WORK
SO FAR ON ME,

519
00:25:45,065 --> 00:25:46,806
I GUESS YOU THINK

520
00:25:46,806 --> 00:25:49,286
I'M VAIN, EGOTISTICAL
AND HATE BEING IGNORED.

521
00:25:49,286 --> 00:25:51,680
DO YOU DISAGREE?

522
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:54,117
NO.
IT'S PRETTY MUCH ACCURATE.HUH.

523
00:25:54,117 --> 00:25:59,340
BUT I'M ALSO CUNNING, RUTHLESS,
AND I HATE TO LOSE.

524
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:02,735
JUST THE KIND OF MAN THAT WOULD
KILL A WOMAN FOR REJECTING HIM.

525
00:26:02,735 --> 00:26:06,129
DID I?WELL, YOU KNEW LISELLE WAS
STUFFED IN THE TRUNK. HOW?

526
00:26:06,129 --> 00:26:08,436
I HAVE A LOT OF FRIENDS--

527
00:26:08,436 --> 00:26:11,395
SHERIFF'S DEPARTMENT,
MAYOR'S OFFICE.DID YOU KILL LISELLE DOUGLAS?

528
00:26:11,395 --> 00:26:13,441
YOU TELL ME.

529
00:26:13,441 --> 00:26:16,444
I'LL KNOW SOON ENOUGH. I JUST
NEED TO READ YOU A LITTLE MORE,

530
00:26:16,444 --> 00:26:20,535
DIG A LITTLE DEEPER INTO
YOUR PSYCHE, IF YOU DON'T MIND.NOT AT ALL. DIG AWAY.
IT'LL BE FUN.

531
00:26:20,535 --> 00:26:22,798
ANYTHING FOR A THRILL.

532
00:26:22,798 --> 00:26:24,757
YES. PRETTY MUCH.[cell phone rings]

533
00:26:24,757 --> 00:26:26,628
HELLO?We brought in
the victim's boyfriend.

534
00:26:26,628 --> 00:26:29,370
HE'S LOOKING PRETTY GOOD
FOR IT.

535
00:26:29,370 --> 00:26:32,591
WANNA COME
AND HAVE A CHAT WITH HIM?Yeah, maybe a little later.
I'm kind of busy.

536
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:35,202
WHERE ARE YOU?WELL, I'M WITH AN ADMIRER
OF YOURS,

537
00:26:35,202 --> 00:26:37,683
WHO, UH, LOOKS VERY GOOD
FOR IT AS WELL,

538
00:26:37,683 --> 00:26:40,686
has "killer"
written all over his face.NOT MASHBURN.

539
00:26:40,686 --> 00:26:44,603
[whispers]
TELL HER I SAID HI.UH, HE SAID HI.

540
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:47,214
[beep]IN THERE.

541
00:26:47,214 --> 00:26:49,172
HUNG UP.

542
00:26:52,654 --> 00:26:54,308
GRACE.YES?

543
00:26:54,308 --> 00:26:57,703
LOOK, YOU'RE GIVING ME
FROSTBITE. CAN WE TALK OR WHAT?

544
00:26:57,703 --> 00:27:00,009
[sighs] SURE. I GUESS.

545
00:27:03,186 --> 00:27:06,059
OKAY, LOOK... [sighs]

546
00:27:06,059 --> 00:27:09,062
I'M SORRY. I WASN'T TRYING
TO SAY THAT YOUR JOB

547
00:27:09,062 --> 00:27:11,238
IS LESS IMPORTANT THAN MINE.

548
00:27:11,238 --> 00:27:13,240
I KNOW. IT'S JUST...

549
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,851
YOU'RE DECIDING
HOW MY CAREER SHOULD GO?

550
00:27:15,851 --> 00:27:18,245
PLANNING MY ENTIRE LIFE
FOR ME?

551
00:27:18,245 --> 00:27:20,421
IT'S NOT LIKE WE'RE MARRIED
OR ANYTHING.

552
00:27:20,421 --> 00:27:23,250
GRACE, I GET IT. YOU'RE RIGHT.
WE'RE NOT MARRIED.

553
00:27:23,250 --> 00:27:26,427
HOW STUPID WOULD THAT BE,
RIGHT?

554
00:27:26,427 --> 00:27:30,779
STUPID?YEAH, UM, WE'VE ONLY BEEN
DATING A COUPLE MONTHS.

555
00:27:30,779 --> 00:27:33,913
WHO KNOWS WHAT'S GONNA HAPPEN?WELL, SURE,
BUT WHAT'S STUPID ABOUT IT?

556
00:27:33,913 --> 00:27:36,829
I-I-I-I MEANT STUPID
IF WE GOT MARRIED TODAY.BUT WHAT ABOUT TOMORROW?

557
00:27:36,829 --> 00:27:39,135
I MEAN, LONG-TERM,
WHERE ARE WE?

558
00:27:39,135 --> 00:27:42,486
DO WE HAVE TO DISCUSS THIS
RIGHT NOW?YEAH, WE PROBABLY
SHOULD HAVE DONE IT

559
00:27:42,486 --> 00:27:44,575
BEFORE WE ANNOUNCED
OUR RELATIONSHIP

560
00:27:44,575 --> 00:27:48,318
AND I ENDANGERED MY JOB.WELL,
MY JOB'S ON THE LINE, TOO.

561
00:27:48,318 --> 00:27:51,278
THAT'S NOT WHAT YOU SAID BEFORE.
YOU HAVE SENIORITY, REMEMBER?LOOK, GRACE,
I KNOW YOU'RE SCARED,

562
00:27:51,278 --> 00:27:54,411
BUT YOU CAN'T KEEP BLOWING
HOT AND COLD ON ME LIKE THIS,

563
00:27:54,411 --> 00:27:57,676
NOT NOW.SO WHAT, I SHOULD JUST MOVE
TO THE FRESNO OFFICE

564
00:27:57,676 --> 00:28:01,680
AND SMILE ABOUT IT?YOU KNOW WHAT? FINE.
DO WHATEVER YOU WANT, GRACE.

565
00:28:03,812 --> 00:28:05,379
[scoffs]

566
00:28:10,253 --> 00:28:13,430
JEFF, WE'VE GOT THE LAB
RUSHING THE RESULTS

567
00:28:13,430 --> 00:28:16,869
ON THE D.N.A. TEST
ON THE BUMPER OF THE FERRARI.

568
00:28:16,869 --> 00:28:19,828
ONCE WE FIND LISELLE'S BLOOD,
ANY LEVERAGE YOU HAD IS GONE.

569
00:28:19,828 --> 00:28:23,049
YOU SHOULD PLEAD THIS OUT NOW.YOU THINK I KILLED HER?

570
00:28:23,049 --> 00:28:25,965
IT HELPS THAT YOU SAID SO
DURING THE STANDOFF.

571
00:28:25,965 --> 00:28:28,619
RIGHT.

572
00:28:28,619 --> 00:28:30,143
WHAT'S WEIRD...

573
00:28:30,143 --> 00:28:32,841
I THINK
IF I HAD KILLED HER,

574
00:28:32,841 --> 00:28:37,237
I'D FEEL BETTER THAN I DO NOW.
AT LEAST I'D FEEL IN CONTROL.

575
00:28:37,237 --> 00:28:39,021
SO NOW YOU'RE SAYING
YOU DIDN'T DO IT?

576
00:28:39,021 --> 00:28:41,154
I DIDN'T.

577
00:28:41,154 --> 00:28:42,764
BUT I DID...

578
00:28:42,764 --> 00:28:45,071
METAPHORICALLY.

579
00:28:45,071 --> 00:28:47,160
I KILLED HER
WITH MY SELFISHNESS.

580
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:49,423
THIS ISN'T A LYRIC-WRITING
WORKSHOP, JEFF.

581
00:28:49,423 --> 00:28:51,860
YOU WERE THERE
THE NIGHT SHE DIED.

582
00:28:51,860 --> 00:28:56,256
YOU STOLE THE CAR AT LANDAU'S
REQUEST AND STASHED IT WHERE?

583
00:28:56,256 --> 00:28:58,040
PARKING GARAGE?

584
00:28:58,040 --> 00:28:59,738
[whispers] YEAH.

585
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:02,741
[normal voice] I THOUGHT, UH,
IF THIS GUY GIVES ME A BREAK,

586
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:06,179
I CAN FINALLY MAKE IT,
TAKE CARE OF LISELLE FOR ONCE.

587
00:29:06,179 --> 00:29:08,616
[scoffs]

588
00:29:08,616 --> 00:29:11,575
SHE TAKES CARE OF ME
BY WORKING HER ASS OFF.

589
00:29:11,575 --> 00:29:13,839
MY BIG IDEA WAS
GRAND THEFT AUTO.

590
00:29:13,839 --> 00:29:17,190
MAYBE LISELLE CAUGHT YOU,
TRIED TO STOP YOU.NO.

591
00:29:17,190 --> 00:29:19,105
MAYBE IT WAS AN ACCIDENT.

592
00:29:19,105 --> 00:29:20,802
NO.

593
00:29:20,802 --> 00:29:24,240
SHE W--SHE NEVER EVEN SAW ME.
SHE WAS WORKING TOO HARD.

594
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:31,421
[voice breaking] I LOVED HER.

595
00:29:31,421 --> 00:29:33,423
IF I HAD KILLED HER,

596
00:29:33,423 --> 00:29:36,600
YOU WOULDN'T BE TALKING TO ME,
'CAUSE I'D BE DEAD, TOO.

597
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:44,173
[lowered voice] WE NEED JANE.[whispers] YEAH.

598
00:29:44,173 --> 00:29:47,220
THE HUMAN BRAIN IS
BUILT IN LAYERS--

599
00:29:47,220 --> 00:29:48,874
THE HOMO SAPIEN BRAIN

600
00:29:48,874 --> 00:29:51,877
ON TOP OF THE CAVEMAN
ON TOP OF THE ANIMAL.

601
00:29:51,877 --> 00:29:54,488
WAY DOWN, DEEP BELOW, YOU WILL
FIND THE LIZARD BRAIN.

602
00:29:54,488 --> 00:29:56,969
LIZARD--
ALL ACTION AND REACTION,

603
00:29:56,969 --> 00:29:58,884
NO SUBTLETY.

604
00:29:58,884 --> 00:30:01,930
YOU CANNOT TRAIN IT
TO NOT REACT.

605
00:30:01,930 --> 00:30:04,628
THEN WHERE DID
I HIDE THE RING?YOU'RE TELLING ME.

606
00:30:04,628 --> 00:30:06,239
[laughs]

607
00:30:06,239 --> 00:30:08,850
ALL THE LIZARD BRAIN KNOWS
IS THAT SOMETHING IS HIDDEN

608
00:30:08,850 --> 00:30:13,202
AND YOU DON'T WANT IT FOUND.
YOU CAN'T HIDE YOUR REACTION.

609
00:30:13,202 --> 00:30:16,510
YOU'RE TALKING A GOOD GAME,
BUT I DON'T SEE MY RING.

610
00:30:16,510 --> 00:30:19,208
I'M LISTENING,
AND THE RING...

611
00:30:19,208 --> 00:30:21,907
IS...

612
00:30:21,907 --> 00:30:24,823
[exhales deeply]

613
00:30:32,961 --> 00:30:35,355
EXCUSE ME.

614
00:30:35,355 --> 00:30:36,878
HUH.

615
00:30:36,878 --> 00:30:38,184
THANKS.

616
00:30:38,184 --> 00:30:39,663
[woman laughs]CHEERS.

617
00:30:43,276 --> 00:30:45,104
THANK YOU.

618
00:30:45,104 --> 00:30:47,280
VOILà.

619
00:30:47,280 --> 00:30:49,021
PARLOR TRICK.

620
00:30:49,021 --> 00:30:52,111
YES, BUT IT GIVES ME
A TRUER SENSE OF YOUR CHARACTER.

621
00:30:52,111 --> 00:30:54,896
IT'S QUACKERY.
YOU--YOU DISAPPOINT ME.

622
00:30:54,896 --> 00:30:58,117
YOU THINK YOU SWEAT TOO MUCH,
YOU HAVE MILD DIRT PHOBIA,

623
00:30:58,117 --> 00:31:00,380
AND YOU HAVE ISSUES
WITH YOUR MOTHER.

624
00:31:00,380 --> 00:31:04,036
WHO DOESN'T? QUACKERY.IF I CARED AT ALL
ABOUT RESPECT,

625
00:31:04,036 --> 00:31:07,169
I WOULD SAY THAT
THAT IS DISRESPECTFUL.I JUST SAY WHAT I SEE.

626
00:31:07,169 --> 00:31:09,215
I HAVE TO PROVE YOU WRONG.

627
00:31:09,215 --> 00:31:11,826
DO YOU HAVE, UH,
A GOOD FAST CAR AVAILABLE?I DO.

628
00:31:11,826 --> 00:31:13,610
MM.

629
00:31:13,610 --> 00:31:15,612
JANE,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

630
00:31:15,612 --> 00:31:17,788
CHO. PROVING A POINT.
LISBON WITH YOU?

631
00:31:17,788 --> 00:31:20,835
NO.OH, THAT'S A SHAME.
SHE'D ENJOY THIS.

632
00:31:20,835 --> 00:31:23,794
SHE WANTS YOU
BACK AT THE OFFICE.NO DOUBT. YOU READY, WALTER?

633
00:31:23,794 --> 00:31:26,797
I THINK SO.GOOD. OH! IT'S VERY LOW.

634
00:31:26,797 --> 00:31:29,322
YOU NERVOUS?OF COURSE NOT.

635
00:31:29,322 --> 00:31:33,108
WELL, YOU SHOULD BE.
IT'S A VERY FANCY CAR.

636
00:31:33,108 --> 00:31:35,241
I DON'T LIKE THE COLOR.

637
00:31:35,241 --> 00:31:38,113
BUT, UH, WHAT I'M GONNA DO
IS STEER

638
00:31:38,113 --> 00:31:40,115
BY FEELING YOUR REACTIONS.

639
00:31:40,115 --> 00:31:42,378
YOU PLAY IT COOL, WE CRASH.

640
00:31:42,378 --> 00:31:46,469
WHATEVER YOU DO,
DO NOT CLOSE YOUR EYES. OKAY?

641
00:31:46,469 --> 00:31:50,821
[birds chirping]

642
00:31:50,821 --> 00:31:52,214
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

643
00:31:52,214 --> 00:31:54,216
UH, HOW DO I TURN IT ON?

644
00:31:54,216 --> 00:31:56,218
HERE.OKAY.

645
00:31:56,218 --> 00:31:58,829
[engine turns on]WHOA.

646
00:31:58,829 --> 00:32:02,268
[engine revving]

647
00:32:02,268 --> 00:32:03,965
[imitates engine revving]

648
00:32:33,777 --> 00:32:35,779
[brakes screech]WHOA!

649
00:32:35,779 --> 00:32:38,739
WHOO!OH, I'LL BE DAMNED. [laughs]

650
00:32:38,739 --> 00:32:42,699
AHH! THAT WAS FUN.

651
00:32:42,699 --> 00:32:45,920
WHOO! [whistles]

652
00:32:45,920 --> 00:32:49,097
THANK YOU. VOILà.
ALL IN THE WRIST.

653
00:32:49,097 --> 00:32:51,056
HUH? ALL IN THE WRIST.[Walter laughs]

654
00:32:51,056 --> 00:32:52,840
[crowd shouts indistinctly]

655
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:54,320
[all gasp]

656
00:32:54,320 --> 00:32:56,235
AAH! OHH!

657
00:32:56,235 --> 00:32:57,497
[thud]

658
00:32:59,368 --> 00:33:02,241
[seagulls calling]

659
00:33:12,860 --> 00:33:15,776
WHY'D YOU DO THAT?

660
00:33:15,776 --> 00:33:17,517
IT WAS A TOTAL ACCIDENT.

661
00:33:17,517 --> 00:33:21,695
AH.

662
00:33:21,695 --> 00:33:23,566
WELL, UH...

663
00:33:23,566 --> 00:33:25,655
AT LEAST NO ONE GOT HURT.

664
00:33:25,655 --> 00:33:26,961
[sniffles]

665
00:33:28,832 --> 00:33:31,400
IT WAS A TERRIBLE COLOR,
ANYWAY.

666
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:34,925
I-I'LL GET YOU A NEW ONE.

667
00:33:34,925 --> 00:33:36,231
SORRY.

668
00:33:47,329 --> 00:33:50,332
NO TRACES OF BLOOD OR D.N.A.
ON THE STOLEN CAR.

669
00:33:50,332 --> 00:33:53,335
NOTHING?
SO WE HAVE NO MURDER WEAPON.AND NO SUSPECTS.

670
00:33:53,335 --> 00:33:56,295
LET'S START OVER. GO THROUGH
EVERY WITNESS STATEMENT.[cell phone rings]

671
00:33:56,295 --> 00:33:58,949
EXCUSE ME. HEY, CHO.

672
00:33:58,949 --> 00:34:01,082
OH, NO.

673
00:34:01,082 --> 00:34:03,084
OH, GREAT.

674
00:34:03,084 --> 00:34:05,043
NO. NO,
YOU CAN HANDLE THIS ONE.

675
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:08,002
JUST BE SURE TO BE CLEAR
THAT THE CBI IS NOT LIABLE.

676
00:34:08,002 --> 00:34:10,396
HE IS JUST A CONSULTANT.

677
00:34:13,094 --> 00:34:15,227
UH, LONG STORY.

678
00:34:15,227 --> 00:34:17,316
UH, I HAVE TO BUY WALTER
A NEW CAR.

679
00:34:17,316 --> 00:34:19,361
COULD YOU SHOW US
WHAT YOU HAVE?

680
00:34:19,361 --> 00:34:22,799
AS I EXPLAINED, MR. JANE,
WE NEED A BANK STATEMENT

681
00:34:22,799 --> 00:34:25,889
TO CONFIRM--MR. JANE HAS ASSURED ME ON HIS
HONOR THAT HE'S GOOD FOR IT.

682
00:34:25,889 --> 00:34:28,153
SO I'LL VOUCH FOR HIM.

683
00:34:28,153 --> 00:34:30,894
DO YOU NEED TO SEE
MYBANK STATEMENT?[laughs] OF COURSE NOT.

684
00:34:30,894 --> 00:34:33,549
ALL RIGHT.
WELL, THEN LET'S DO THIS.ABSOLUTELY.

685
00:34:33,549 --> 00:34:36,683
I THINK WE'LL HAVE ELIAS
SHOW US AROUND.BUT YOU WANT THE BEST
TO HELP SHOW YOU AROUND.

686
00:34:36,683 --> 00:34:40,991
YES, HE'S SECOND BEST.
HE'LL TRY HARDER.

687
00:34:40,991 --> 00:34:43,255
RIGHT?RIGHT.

688
00:34:43,255 --> 00:34:45,126
SHALL WE?

689
00:34:50,871 --> 00:34:54,179
HOW ABOUT THIS ONE HERE?EXCELLENT EYE. THIS CAR--

690
00:34:54,179 --> 00:34:58,487
WELL, IT'S GRAY.
I MEAN, REALLY? GRAY?

691
00:34:58,487 --> 00:35:00,489
YOUR CAR.

692
00:35:00,489 --> 00:35:01,882
MM.

693
00:35:01,882 --> 00:35:04,014
NO.

694
00:35:04,014 --> 00:35:08,106
GRAY'D BE COMPLETELY WRONG,
WOULDN'T IT?

695
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:11,457
LET'S TAKE A LOOK
AT THE, UH...

696
00:35:11,457 --> 00:35:13,981
ACTUALLY, NO.
LET'S GO THIS WAY. SHALL WE?

697
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:21,510
PATRICK, WE'VE BEEN THIS WAY
BEFORE. LET'S GO BACK.

698
00:35:21,510 --> 00:35:24,122
OH, PLEASE. BE PATIENT.
SEE, THE THING IS, WALTER,

699
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:26,254
NO MATTER HOW SMART A PLAN
YOU MAKE,

700
00:35:26,254 --> 00:35:29,257
THERE IS ALWAYS SOMEONE SMARTER
WHO WILL SEE THROUGH IT--

701
00:35:29,257 --> 00:35:31,825
MAKES IT VERY HARD
TO GET AWAY WITH MURDER.

702
00:35:36,177 --> 00:35:39,137
I LIKE THIS CAR SHOPPING.
IT'S A LOT OF FUN.

703
00:35:48,581 --> 00:35:51,671
I THINK THAT'S YOUR CAR.

704
00:35:51,671 --> 00:35:53,673
WHAT DO YOU THINK, CHO?

705
00:35:53,673 --> 00:35:55,892
6-SPEED, PEDAL SHIFTERS.
NICE.

706
00:35:55,892 --> 00:35:57,329
OH, YEAH. MM!

707
00:35:57,329 --> 00:35:59,418
EH. IT'S OKAY, I SUPPOSE.

708
00:35:59,418 --> 00:36:02,116
TRY IT.
I THINK YOU'LL LIKE IT.

709
00:36:02,116 --> 00:36:04,510
I'LL TAKE A LOOK.MR. MASHBURN,
MAY I SUGGEST--

710
00:36:04,510 --> 00:36:07,252
THIS CAR--IT'S...
A LITTLE GAUCHE FOR YOU.

711
00:36:07,252 --> 00:36:09,950
DID YOU SEE HIS LAST CAR?

712
00:36:09,950 --> 00:36:12,082
THIS IS A LOT BETTER COLOR.

713
00:36:12,082 --> 00:36:14,128
THIS COLOR SYMBOLIZES
PASSION, LUST, ANGER.

714
00:36:14,128 --> 00:36:15,912
I THINK IT'S LOVELY.

715
00:36:15,912 --> 00:36:19,960
IT DOES HAVE A LITTLE DING
DOWN HERE.

716
00:36:19,960 --> 00:36:23,833
I'M SURE THEY CAN FIX THAT,
RIGHT, ELIAS?

717
00:36:23,833 --> 00:36:27,402
IT'S A REALLY NICE CAR, BUT IT'S
HAD SOME TRANSMISSION PROBLEMS.

718
00:36:27,402 --> 00:36:30,318
I SUGGEST THAT WE LOOK
AT THE LAMBORGHINI MURCIéLAGO.

719
00:36:30,318 --> 00:36:31,972
V-12,

720
00:36:31,972 --> 00:36:35,105
631 HORSEPOWER--MUCH NICER
THAN THE ONE YOU HAD BEFORE.

721
00:36:35,105 --> 00:36:36,846
YOU KNOW WHAT?

722
00:36:36,846 --> 00:36:39,849
MAYBE--MAYBE WE LEFT THE FIRST
FLOOR A LITTLE TOO SOON.

723
00:36:39,849 --> 00:36:42,765
THERE WERE SOME REALLY CHOICE
CARS UPSTAIRS.

724
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:48,684
BUT, OF COURSE, IF THIS IS
THE CAR YOU LIKE, NO PROBLEM.

725
00:36:48,684 --> 00:36:50,382
OF COURSE. [chuckles]

726
00:36:50,382 --> 00:36:53,776
I MEAN, IT'S--IT'S A MATTER
OF OPINION. I...

727
00:36:56,083 --> 00:36:59,782
YOU FEELING ALL RIGHT?I'M FINE, YES.
THAT'S--I'M FINE.

728
00:36:59,782 --> 00:37:01,567
HE'S NOT FINE.

729
00:37:01,567 --> 00:37:04,222
HE'S FEELING SQUEAMISH
'CAUSE THIS IS THE CAR

730
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:06,267
THAT HE USED TO KILL LISELLE.I'M SORRY. WHAT?

731
00:37:06,267 --> 00:37:08,617
YOU LED US RIGHT TO IT.I DID NOT.

732
00:37:08,617 --> 00:37:11,098
YES, YOU DID.
YOU LED US RIGHT TO IT,

733
00:37:11,098 --> 00:37:15,233
AND HOW COULD YOU DO THAT
IF YOU DIDN'T KILL HER?[laughs] THAT'S THE MOST--

734
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:17,147
THAT'S THE MOST RIDICULOUS...

735
00:37:18,975 --> 00:37:22,457
THIS CAR WAS THE HIDDEN RING,
WASN'T IT?YEP.

736
00:37:22,457 --> 00:37:25,721
AND YOU READ ELIAS' LIZARD BRAIN
TO FIGURE OUT--YEAH.

737
00:37:29,116 --> 00:37:31,423
[grunts]

738
00:37:31,423 --> 00:37:33,773
[grunts]

739
00:37:33,773 --> 00:37:37,603
[panting]

740
00:37:37,603 --> 00:37:40,693
[handcuffs click]

741
00:37:40,693 --> 00:37:42,260
SO IT'S OVER.

742
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,957
YEAH, IT'S OVER.

743
00:37:43,957 --> 00:37:46,438
THAT'S TOO BAD.
IT WAS FUN.

744
00:37:46,438 --> 00:37:49,136
YEAH. HOW YOU GONNA TOP
THAT THRILL?

745
00:37:49,136 --> 00:37:51,747
MAYBE NEXT TIME
I'LL BE THE KILLER.

746
00:37:54,228 --> 00:37:56,012
IT'S THE COMPETITION.

747
00:37:56,012 --> 00:37:58,363
YOU HAVE NO IDEA.
IT EATS AT YOU.

748
00:37:58,363 --> 00:38:01,540
SECOND PLACE--FIRST LOSER.

749
00:38:01,540 --> 00:38:03,498
KINSEY WAS WINNING
ANOTHER SALES DRIVE.

750
00:38:03,498 --> 00:38:05,457
IT SHOULD HAVE BEEN YOU.

751
00:38:05,457 --> 00:38:07,415
WESTHOFF LIKES HUSTLE,
SO YOU HUSTLED.

752
00:38:07,415 --> 00:38:10,244
AND YOU MADE KINSEY SICK

753
00:38:10,244 --> 00:38:12,246
BY POISONING
HIS BEEF BARLEY SOUP.

754
00:38:12,246 --> 00:38:14,901
ONLY LISELLE CAUGHT YOU
AT IT, DIDN'T SHE?

755
00:38:25,477 --> 00:38:27,479
KINSEY HAD BEEN SICK
FOR A WHILE.

756
00:38:27,479 --> 00:38:29,785
SHE FIGURED IT OUT,
GOT MAD.

757
00:38:29,785 --> 00:38:32,788
SHE THREW AWAY THE SOUP
AND SAID THAT I HAD TO TELL

758
00:38:32,788 --> 00:38:35,748
WESTHOFF WHAT I HAD DONE, TOLD
ME I HAD TO MAKE THIS RIGHT.

759
00:38:35,748 --> 00:38:38,272
"MAKE THIS RIGHT"--
WHO SAYS THAT?

760
00:38:38,272 --> 00:38:41,971
SELF-RIGHTEOUS BITCH.

761
00:38:41,971 --> 00:38:45,758
WESTHOFF FINDS OUT I WAS
TAKING OUT HIS TOP EARNER,

762
00:38:45,758 --> 00:38:48,674
HE'D MAKE SURE
I'D NEVER WORK AGAIN.

763
00:38:48,674 --> 00:38:52,504
AND KINSEY? THAT SON OF A BITCH WOULD CALL THE COPS FOR SURE.[tires peal]

764
00:38:54,375 --> 00:38:55,898
[thump]

765
00:38:55,898 --> 00:38:57,900
SECURITY SHOWED UP
SOONER THAN I THOUGHT,

766
00:38:57,900 --> 00:38:59,946
SO I STUFFED THE BODY
IN THE TRUNK.

767
00:38:59,946 --> 00:39:02,557
IT WAS ME OR HER.

768
00:39:02,557 --> 00:39:04,603
YOU HAVE TO UNDERSTAND THAT.

769
00:39:04,603 --> 00:39:07,606
SOMEONE GIVES YOU THAT CHOICE,
YOU CHOOSE YOU EVERY TIME.

770
00:39:07,606 --> 00:39:10,957
I'M SURE A JURY
WILL SYMPATHIZE.

771
00:39:10,957 --> 00:39:13,133
HOW DID YOU KNOW IT WAS ME?

772
00:39:13,133 --> 00:39:15,527
LIKE I SAID,
YOU'RE NUMBER TWO.

773
00:39:15,527 --> 00:39:17,920
NUMBER TWO
ALWAYS TRIES HARDER.

774
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:21,750
THAT, AND NOBODY STEALS
BEEF BARLEY SOUP.

775
00:39:26,929 --> 00:39:30,150
THEY, UH, TOLD ME
THEY'RE NOT PRESSING CHARGES,

776
00:39:30,150 --> 00:39:32,152
SAID I HAVE YOU TO THANK.

777
00:39:32,152 --> 00:39:35,938
SO, UH, YOU KNOW, THANKS.

778
00:39:35,938 --> 00:39:38,114
JUST DON'T SCREW IT UP,
JEFF.

779
00:39:51,127 --> 00:39:53,173
YOU DIDN'T TELL ME.

780
00:39:53,173 --> 00:39:56,045
EXCUSE ME?THAT YOU'RE TOGETHER.
YOU DIDN'T SAY IT.

781
00:39:56,045 --> 00:39:58,047
I DIDN'T HEAR YOU.

782
00:39:58,047 --> 00:40:00,310
THERE ARE NO RULES BEING BROKEN
THAT I'M AWARE OF--

783
00:40:00,310 --> 00:40:03,966
NO HOLDING HANDS,
NO SOULFUL LOOKS

784
00:40:03,966 --> 00:40:06,795
AND ABSOLUTELY NO KISSING
IN THE OFFICE.NO PROBLEM.

785
00:40:06,795 --> 00:40:07,970
FINE.

786
00:40:13,585 --> 00:40:16,370
[cell phone rings]

787
00:40:16,370 --> 00:40:17,980
HELLO?

788
00:40:17,980 --> 00:40:19,591
JANE?

789
00:40:19,591 --> 00:40:21,419
MEET YOU WHERE?

790
00:40:25,988 --> 00:40:28,817
HEY. NEED A RIDE?

791
00:40:28,817 --> 00:40:30,819
WHERE DID YOU GET THAT?

792
00:40:30,819 --> 00:40:33,518
OH, THIS OLD THING?
WALTER MASHBURN.

793
00:40:33,518 --> 00:40:35,433
EVEN THOUGH
YOU WRECKED HIS CAR

794
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:38,087
JUST TO GET A CLEAN READ
ON ELIAS?IS THAT WHAT I DID?

795
00:40:38,087 --> 00:40:41,308
YEAH, YOU DID.
MASHBURN'S NOT MAD?NO. WE GAVE HIM
A NEW EXPERIENCE.

796
00:40:41,308 --> 00:40:44,180
HE HELPED US
CATCH THE KILLER.

797
00:40:44,180 --> 00:40:48,358
THIS IS HIS WAY OF SAYING
THANK YOU. GET IN.WE'RE NOT ALLOWED
TO ACCEPT GIFTS FROM PEOPLE.

798
00:40:48,358 --> 00:40:50,360
IT'S NOT A GIFT.
IT'S A LEND.

799
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:53,015
NOW I KNOW THIS FANTASTIC
RESTAURANT IN NAPA.

800
00:40:53,015 --> 00:40:56,628
WE CAN BE THERE IN ABOUT
SEVEN AND A HALF MINUTES.

801
00:40:56,628 --> 00:40:59,326
IT'LL BLOW YOUR MIND.IT IS A PRETTY NICE CAR.

802
00:40:59,326 --> 00:41:01,589
YES, IT IS. COME ON.

803
00:41:06,072 --> 00:41:08,422
PROMISE YOU WON'T
BREAK THE SPEED LIMIT?

804
00:41:08,422 --> 00:41:10,206
NOPE.

805
00:41:10,206 --> 00:41:12,121
[tires peal][Lisbon] OOH!

806
00:41:21,174 --> 00:41:23,959
STAY TUNED FOR SCENES
FROM OUR NEXT EPISODE.

